Let $s$, $k \in \mathbb{N}^+$, let $\varnothing\neq W \subset \Gamma$ be a finite set, and let $\mathcal{P} \subseteq k^W$. Suppose that
       \begin{equation}
            \mathsf{e}^{s+1} \left(1 - \frac{|\mathcal{P}|}{k^{|W|}}\right) |W|^{2(s+1)} \,\leqslant\, 1.
       \end{equation}
       Then every free zero-dimensional Polish $\Gamma$-space $X$ 
       such that $\mathsf{asi}_{\mathsf{c}}(X) \leqslant s$ admits a continuous $\Gamma$-equivariant map $\pi \colon X \to \Sigma(k, W, \mathcal{P})$.
